{"y":2001,"label":"2000–01","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East MBB East","confShort":"Big East MBB East","w":20,"l":12,"cw":8,"cl":8,"confFinish":"6th in Big East MBB East","finish":"nit","apPre":14,"apHigh":10,"srs":10.17,"sos":5.43,"ortg":106.1,"drtg":98.8,"ppg":73.4,"oppg":68.3,"story":{"headline":"Enter Caron Butler","text":"A retooled roster leaned on freshman Caron Butler, who led the Huskies in scoring (15.3) and rebounding (7.6) and made the Big East All-Freshman team, and on freshman point guard Taliek Brown, who started every game. UConn beat No. 5 Arizona 71–69, No. 9 Boston College 82–71 — Brown scored 21 that night — and No. 13 Notre Dame 75–59, but finished just 20–12 and 8–8 in the Big East. Syracuse ended the Huskies' Big East tournament in the first round, 86–75, sending UConn to the NIT, where it beat South Carolina 72–65 before losing to Detroit 67–61. Brown also dished a season-best 12 assists in an overtime win over St. John's, and the Huskies went 8–1 at Gampel. It was the program's only NIT trip between 1998 and 2009.","moments":[{"date":"2001-03-18","title":"NIT Second Round: L vs Detroit","text":"UConn lost to Detroit 61–67 (Second Round) at Harry A. Gampel Pavilion, Storrs, Connecticut."}],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000%E2%80%9301_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caron_Butler","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taliek_Brown"]},"roster":[{"pid":"albert-mouring-1","name":"Albert Mouring","num":"23","cls":"SR","pos":"G","ht":"6-3","wt":180,"home":"Preston, MD","pg":{"g":32,"gs":32,"mp":34.4,"pts":15.1,"trb":3.2,"ast":1.7,"stl":1.2,"blk":0.4,"tov":1.6,"fg_pct":0.437,"fg3_pct":0.374,"ft_pct":0.889,"orb":0.8,"pf":1.7},"tot":{"mp":1101,"fg":160,"fga":366,"fg3":58,"fg3a":155,"ft":104,"fta":117,"orb":26,"drb":75,"trb":101,"ast":55,"stl":38,"blk":12,"tov":52,"pf":53,"pts":482,"g":32},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.572,"efg_pct":0.51